{
 "result": "squeeze.py is an LZMA2 raw-format compressor (preset 9e, 1 MB dictionary, header byte picks the best of five lc/lp/pb sets). It round-trips both public samples (ratios about 4.2 and 7.2) and is registered as baseline 5.47469 with 0% noise. The only lever I found that looked worthwhile was priming with other sample text (about 3.5% smaller on in-1 when primed with in-0). Python's lzma module has no preset-dictionary option, so using it would need a custom codec. I judged that too costly for an uncertain gain on hidden inputs, so I am stopping here with about 246 energy unspent.",
